\title{eventclock: The Event Clock: Information Time from Traded Event State Prices}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Measure information arrival ("event-clock time") ahead of scheduled events from traded event state prices such as prediction market contracts. Provides normalization of raw state prices into state-price-implied event probabilities, realized-variation estimators of the information clock A based on the quadratic variation of log-odds (with truncation, bipower, and largest-move robustness variants and a real-time forecast rule), closed-form calculators for the exact logistic-normal transition law, simulation tools, plotting helpers, a connector for the public 'Polymarket' APIs, and the Brexit 2016 and U.S. election 2016 event-probability series that reproduce the headline estimates in Hanke, Schadner, Stöckl, and Weissensteiner (Working Paper) "Learning Before Scheduled Events: Prediction Markets, State Prices, and Option Valuation".
}
